## Control {{controlId}}: Monitor and Control Remote Access Sessions

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization monitors and controls remote access sessions within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant. Remote access monitoring is implemented through Conditional Access policies, named location definitions, sign-in log analysis, and Microsoft Sentinel SIEM correlation that provides continuous visibility into remote authentication activity.

{{#if conditionalAccessActive}}
Conditional Access policies across {{caPoliciesTotalCount}} configurations enforce remote access controls. All remote sessions require multi-factor authentication and device compliance verification before granting access. Policies differentiate between corporate network locations and external access points, applying stricter controls for sessions originating outside trusted boundaries.
{{else}}
Conditional Access policies for remote access monitoring have not been configured. Remote access relies on standard Azure AD authentication pending enhanced policy deployment.
{{/if}}

{{#if namedLocationsConfigured}}
{{namedLocationsCount}} named locations define trusted network boundaries for remote access classification. Sessions from untrusted locations trigger additional authentication requirements and enhanced logging for security monitoring.
{{/if}}

{{#if signInLogsAvailable}}
Sign-in logs capture {{signInLogsCount}} authentication events, providing audit trail for all remote access sessions including source IP, device compliance status, and authentication method used.
{{/if}}

